    <artifactId>kompile-app-web-admin</artifactId>
    <name>Kompile App - Admin Console Web Layer</name>
    <description>
        The admin persona web layer — everything that is not an end-user surface: nd4j and GPU
        diagnostics, model staging and the model registry, VLM and Triton, benchmarks, the scheduler
        and subprocess management, the enforcer, MCP administration and tool permissions, install and
        backup, experiments and evaluation, and graph maintenance/rules/health/simulator/OWL.

        85 controllers plus the 32 support types only they reach: the diagram, monitor and
        allocation-diagnostics domains, the git diff services, and the backup/benchmark/sdx/writeback
        services. Mounted only by kompile-app-main.

        Packages are preserved (ai.kompile.app.web.controllers, ai.kompile.app.diagram,
        ai.kompile.app.monitor, ai.kompile.app.diagnostics, ai.kompile.app.services...) — the move is
        git mv plus pom wiring, so native-image reflect/resource config and every existing import are
        unaffected. Isolation comes from classpath presence, not package naming.

        Verified zero back-edges into kompile-app-main: the closure is transitive, so every app-main
        type an admin controller reaches came with it. What stays behind in app-main is application
        wiring — MainApplication, the @Configuration classes, the SPI implementations, the subprocess
        launchers, and the MCP @Tool classes, which reach admin controllers in the legal direction
        because app-main depends on this module.

        See docs/architecture/app-persona-boundary.md.
    </description>

